,"model_generated":false,"confidence":1.0,"rationale":"the patch modified protected paths, which fails the task regardless of test results: tests/test_acceptance_slug_collapse.py","evidence_refs":{"run_id":"bff8a68b4ece40caaf64e4a06fa1a248","outcome":"unsolved","layer_statuses":{"environment":"passed","patch":"failed"},"violations":["tests/test_acceptance_slug_collapse.py"]},"author":null,"supersedes_id":null,"superseded":false,"created_at":"2026-10-29T14:14:32.567957"}],"attempt_history":[],"event_count":17,"resources":null,"task_snapshot":{"schema_version":"1.0","task_id":"textkit-slugify-collapse","version":"1.0","title":"slugify emits repeated and dangling separators","description":"slugify maps every non-alphanumeric character to the separator individually, so runs of punctuation or whitespace produce repeated separators and the result can start or end with one.","problem_statement":"`textkit.slugify` produces malformed slugs.\n\nReproduction:\n\n    >>> from textkit import slugify\n    >>> slugify(\"Hello,  World!\")\n    'hello---world-'\n\nExpected: 'hello-world'\n\nThe function should treat a *run* of non-alphanumeric characters as a single separator, and the returned slug must not begin or end with a separator. A string with no alphanumeric characters at all should produce an empty slug. This must work for any single-character separator passed via the `sep` argument, not just the default '-'.\n\nDo not change the existing public signature or the ValueError raised for a multi-character separator.","repo":{"kind":"local_path","path":"textkit","revision":"local","subdir":null},"category":"bug_fix","difficulty":"easy","tags":["string-handling","bug-fix","python"],"environment":{"image":"agentbench/benchmark-python:3.12","setup_commands":["python -m pytest --version"],"env":{},"workdir":"/workspace/repo","pip_packages":[]},"tests":{"runner":"pytest","command":"python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider -q --tb=short {selection}","fail_to_pass":["tests/test_acceptance_slug_collapse.py::test_collapses_repeated_separators","tests/test_acceptance_slug_collapse.py::test_strips_leading_and_trailing_separators","tests/test_acceptance_slug_collapse.py::test_punctuation_runs_collapse","tests/test_acceptance_slug_collapse.py::test_only_punctuation_yields_empty_slug","tests/test_acceptance_slug_collapse.py::test_custom_separator_also_collapses"],"pass_to_pass":["tests/test_slug.py::test_lowercases_words","tests/test_slug.py::test_single_space_becomes_separator","tests/test_slug.py::test_custom_separator","tests/test_slug.py::test_digits_are_kept","tests/test_slug.py::test_rejects_multi_character_separator"]},"grading":{"version":"1.0","acceptance_tests":{"tests/test_acceptance_slug_collapse.py":"\"\"\"Hidden acceptance tests for task ``textkit-slugify-collapse``.\n\nStored outside the benchmark repository so the agent never sees it: this\ndirectory is not copied into the sandbox during the agent phase. The grading\nengine injects the file into the workspace immediately before running tests.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom textkit import slugify\n\n\ndef test_collapses_repeated_separators():\n    assert slugify(\"Hello,  World!\") == \"hello-world\"\n\n\ndef test_strips_leading_and_trailing_separators():\n    assert slugify(\"  Hello  \") == \"hello\"\n\n\ndef test_punctuation_runs_collapse():\n    assert slugify(\"a---b\") == \"a-b\"\n\n\ndef test_only_punctuation_yields_empty_slug():\n    assert slugify(\"!!!\") == \"\"\n\n\ndef test_custom_separator_also_collapses():\n    assert slugify(\"Hello,  World!\", sep=\"_\") == \"hello_world\""},"require_non_empty_patch":true,"forbidden_paths":["**/conftest.py","pyproject.toml","pytest.ini","setup.cfg","tests/**","tests/test_acceptance_slug_collapse.py","tox.ini"],"verify_baseline":true,"static_checks":[],"judge":{"enabled":false,"rubric":"","model":null}},"limits":{"agent_timeout_s":600,"setup_timeout_s":180,"test_timeout_s":180,"memory_mb":1024,"cpus":1.0,"disk_mb":4096,"network":"none","max_agent_steps":40}